@host = http://localhost:5000
@ghostId = 64b7f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0

# Tests for  DELETE /api/v1/products/:id/image  (remove a picture, with no new picture).
#
# BEFORE YOU START:
#   - http/test-image.jpg must exist (see the top of product-images.http)
#   - Run test A and test B in auth.http, then S1-S4 in products.http (this gives managerToken, adminToken, userToken)
#   - Access tokens last 15 minutes
#
# Look in Cloudinary > Assets > e-commerce-api/products: write down how many files are there before IMGDEL3.


### IMGDEL1. Manager creates a product (no image) -> 201, saves imageDelProductId
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "picture test lamp",
  "price": 4999,
  "description": "A lamp for testing picture removal.",
  "category": "office",
  "company": "ikea",
  "inventory": 3
}

> {%
    client.global.set('imageDelProductId', response.body.product.id)
%}

### IMGDEL2. Remove the image of a product that has none -> 404 "Product has no image"
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{imageDelProductId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### IMGDEL3. Give it an image -> 200 (Cloudinary folder: one more file than before)
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{imageDelProductId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="test-image.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./test-image.jpg
--WebAppBoundary--


### -------- who may remove, and bad ids --------

### IMGDEL4. No token -> 401
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{imageDelProductId}}/image

### IMGDEL5. Sara (normal user) -> 403
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{imageDelProductId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### IMGDEL6. A product that does not exist -> 404 "Product not found"
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{ghostId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### IMGDEL7. Broken id -> 400 "Invalid value for _id"
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/products/abc/image
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}


### -------- the real removal --------

### IMGDEL8. Manager removes the image -> 200, the product in the answer has NO "image" key
# Cloudinary folder: back to the number of files from before IMGDEL3 (the file was deleted).
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{imageDelProductId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### IMGDEL9. Read the product -> 200, still no "image" key
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{imageDelProductId}}

### IMGDEL10. Remove again -> 404 "Product has no image"
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{imageDelProductId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### IMGDEL11. Upload a new image after removing -> 200 with a link (works from a clean state)
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{imageDelProductId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="test-image.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./test-image.jpg
--WebAppBoundary--

### IMGDEL12. Admin removes it too -> 200, no "image" key (admins may do everything managers may)
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{imageDelProductId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### -------- cleanup --------

### IMGDEL13. Admin deletes the test product -> 200 {"msg":"Product removed"}
# Cloudinary folder: the same number of files as at the start. Nothing is left behind.
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/products/{{imageDelProductId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
